course: dictionary
lesson: 2679
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word around it is the clue. «Dear Diary, today was the WORST.» Words like Dear and today show a personal book of daily thoughts.
explain: The word diary has two meanings. The first is a book where you write what happens each day and how you feel. The second is a book or calendar where you write plans and appointments, like a homework diary that shows when each task is due.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the writer doing? If they tell us what happened and how they felt, it is the first meaning. If they write down dates and plans, it is the second. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A diary is a book where you write what happens each day and how you feel.
fact: A diary can also be a book or calendar where you write plans and appointments, such as a homework diary.
fact: «Dear Diary, today was the WORST.» is a personal and chatty diary entry.
fact: In 1522 the ship Victoria came home with 18 men, and «they found their diaries were one day behind.»
fact: Diaries are useful records: historians can test what people claim with a diary and old records. The plural of diary is diaries.
exercise: «Dear Diary, today was the WORST.» What kind of diary is this? | *A personal book of what happened and how the writer felt | A map of the town | A list of shopping | A book of plans and appointments
exercise: Mia's homework diary shows when each task is due. What is the diary used for here? | Drawing pictures of her friends | Keeping old ship records | Writing about her feelings each day | *Writing down plans and dates
exercise: In «Dear Diary, today was the WORST», which word shows that the entry is about one day? | Diary | WORST | Dear | *today
test: Which is the plural of diary? | *diaries | diary's | diarys | diarie
test: Which meaning of diary fits a calendar of appointments? | *A book or calendar of plans | A kind of fish | A type of cake | A book of daily feelings
exam: Lena writes «Dear Diary, I felt sad today» every night. Which meaning of diary is she using? | *A book of what happens each day and how you feel | A book of plans and appointments | A calendar of school holidays | A map of the park
